# Context filter for builds rooted at the repository.
#
# `scripts/verify/cargo-verify.sh` builds the verification image from here because
# `scripts/guard/check-container-runtime-policy.sh` requires a literal repository-relative context,
# and the image has to copy `rust-toolchain.toml` — the single toolchain pin (ADR-0001 §3), which
# lives at the root and must not be duplicated into a build directory.
#
# Everything is excluded and the two files that image needs are added back, so the daemon receives a
# few kilobytes instead of the whole tree (89MB, including per-area `target/` directories). A build
# that needs more from the root has to say so here, which is the point: a context is auditable.
*
!rust-toolchain.toml
!tools/verify-image/Dockerfile
# The checksum-pinned actionlint release and the script that fetches it. The image warms that
# script's cache at build time so `workflow-policy` can run with no network; copying the version and
# checksum into the Dockerfile instead would put the pin in two places.
!tools/actionlint.env
!scripts/ci/actionlint.sh
# Foundation's Node suite is fetched into the offline verification image from its lockfile. No
# source enters the image; the current source is still supplied by the audited /work bind at run time.
!platforms/foundation-platform/services/foundation-profile-gateway/package.json
!platforms/foundation-platform/services/foundation-profile-gateway/pnpm-lock.yaml
